Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         git
Conflicts: gittree, gitree
Replaces: gittree, gitree
Description: git history of the refs that you tick
 gitrl-f shows the history of a git repository in a window, the way gitg
 draws it, with a checkbox for each branch, remote branch and tag. Only the
 commits that a ticked ref reaches are drawn, and only the ticked refs are
 labelled.
 .
 Names with slashes fold into groups, a click on a commit shows its
 details and its diff, and a path keeps only the commits that change a file
 or a folder. The window follows the repository as it changes.
 .
 gitrl-f is read only: it never writes to the repository. The command line
 is gitrlf.
